{"id": "EUVD-2026-103918", "enisaUuid": "c7ffe460-d983-39d6-9889-e9a39ce0f138", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: imu: adis16400: fix unprotected debugfs reads\n\nadis16400_serial_number_fops is open coded and never calls\ndebugfs_file_get(), so debugfs_remove_recursive() does not wait for a\nread in progress and unbind frees the iio_dev underneath it.\n\nCommit ae1d37a9bb4b (\"iio: imu: adis16400: use DEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE\ninstead of DEFINE_SIMPLE_ATTRIBUTE\") converted product_id and\nflash_count to DEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE, which protects itself, but\nmoved all three files to debugfs_create_file_unsafe().\n\nserial_number prints three registers as \"%.4x-%.4x-%.4x\" and\nDEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE() formats a single u64, so it cannot be\nconverted without changing what the file returns. adis16475 and\nadis16550 already use debugfs_create_file() for their open coded\nfiles. Use it here too.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3078aaef8af4648f94eeafde4b7b36efd9838d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9b4c00f775a915b759b08bfe2c5e806a8301a59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50e8d70ba0743f88afd7e49f9cebd1841ee677f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f501302ebb9e1504162351b951fe3ae331c852ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d94787287a113a1326211647d5e0deed1e9de105"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w4fg-xq8w-gq57", "CVE-2026-98664"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06a3b9ce-dc57-305b-82db-f2cb95c8b8fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "07f132c9-b975-31b1-b92f-ad6bc31bf4e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "0d80289a-7f1a-3d60-b7dd-323bea8ef73f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae1d37a9bb4bd8d9091a40d153143e99b1